UID:10006089-1792832400-1792843200@sdlancaster.org
SUMMARY:McCaskey East Tree Planting & Celebration Event
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a tree planting and celebration event at McCaskey East! \n\n\n\n\nWe are excited to honor Brother Frank with our next tree planting! We need lots of help to plant\, mulch and stake over 200 native trees. These trees will help make McCaskey East be an even happier place for students and our wild critter friends like birds and butterflies! \nThis project is supported by: \n\nLet’s Go 1-2-3 and the McCaskey East Tree Team\nthe Mira Lloyd Dock Award which gave money to Keisha and Tarsha Scovens and Marlisa Yoder-Bontrager for tree planting\nfree trees an supplies from a Pennsylvania Interfaith Power & Light and the Conestoga River Club thanks to private donors\nthe Frank Albrecht Memorial fund through the Lancaster Education Foundation. This fund honors the late Frank Albrecht who passionately made a difference in the lives of McCaskey students\, fellow teachers\, and his community. We’ll have a brief celebration and light refreshments in honor of Frank before our tree planting. Learn more about his impact to SDoL and our community below.\n\nIf you’ve never planted a tree before\, no problem! Tree experts will show us how to plant and tell us more about the native trees we’re putting in the ground. \nCheck out the map of where we’re planting. See planting Areas along Grofftown Run and McCaskey Avenue. \nPick up a FREE native tree or shrub to take home! Plus\, learn more about native trees and shrubs in Lancaster. \nVolunteers are needed to: \n\ndig holes and plant native trees (small to large potted trees and shrubs)\nstake trees\nmulch trees\nwater trees\n\nWhat to bring if you have them: (we will have extra tools and gloves available) \n\nshovel\nwork gloves\nwater bottle\na smile (required)\n\nWhat else? Dress for the weather. Wear protective shoes. \nWeather plan: If it’s rainy or there is inclement we’ll postpone until Saturday\, October 31\, 2026 from 9 am – Noon. \nContacts: \nLydia Martin\, Let’s Go 1-2-3\, cell: 717-475-3964 text or email: lydia@letsgo123.org \nThank you to our McCaskey Tree Team & community partners: \n\nLet’s Go 1-2-3\n\n\nFrank Albrecht Memorial – Lancaster Education Foundation\nSchool District of Lancaster\nPennsylvania Interfaith Power & Light – Roots\, Branches & Hands tree initiative\nConestoga River Club\nAlliance for the Chesapeake Bay – Forestry & Lawn Conversion\nCity of Lancaster\n\nWe extend our grattitude to funding partners and private donors: Lancaster County Community Foundation\, Lancaster Clean Water Partners\, and The Campbell Foundation for supporting our work to increase urban tree canopy for the health and well-being of our Lancaster community. \n\n\n\nSIGN UP HERE: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/mccaskey-east-tree-planting-celebration-event-tickets-2002620462713 
URL:https://sdlancaster.org/event/mccaskey-east-tree-planting-celebration-event/
LOCATION:JP McCaskey High School\,McCaskey East HS\, United States
CATEGORIES:McCaskey,McCaskey Campus
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:School District of Lancaster
